{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"899","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Segments Removal"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya has an array of integers of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya performs the following operations on the array: on each step he finds the longest segment of consecutive equal integers (the leftmost, if there are several such segments) and removes it. For example, if Vasya's array is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[13, 13, 7, 7, 7, 2, 2, 2]"},{"kind":"text","text":", then after one operation it becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[13, 13, 2, 2, 2]"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Compute the number of operations Vasya should make until the array becomes empty, i.e. Vasya removes all elements from it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a sequence "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — Vasya's array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of operations Vasya should make to remove all elements from the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n2 5 5 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n6 3 4 1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n4 4 4 2 2 100 100 100\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n10 10 50 10 50 50\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, at first Vasya removes two fives at the second and third positions. The array becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[2, 2]"},{"kind":"text","text":". In the second operation Vasya removes two twos at the first and second positions. After that the array becomes empty."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example Vasya has to perform five operations to make the array empty. In each of them he removes the first element from the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example Vasya needs three operations. In the first operation he removes all integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":", in the second — all integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":", in the third — all integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth example in the first operation Vasya removes the first two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":". After that the array becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[50, 10, 50, 50]"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then in the second operation Vasya removes the two rightmost integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50"},{"kind":"text","text":", so that the array becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[50, 10]"},{"kind":"text","text":". In the third operation he removes the remaining "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"50"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the array becomes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"[10]"},{"kind":"text","text":" after that. In the last, fourth operation he removes the only remaining "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":". The array is empty after that."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"899E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/899/problem/E"}